{"request_uuid": "ce794cda-7704-4462-a744-ff62d48b00d8", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T08:45:53.368401+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "planning", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_update", "usage": {"input": 1060, "output": 744, "cacheRead": 104960, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 598, "totalTokens": 106764, "cost": {"input": 0.000318, "output": 0.0008927999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.00062976, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.00184056}}, "assistantMessageEvent": {"type": "thinking_end", "contentIndex": 0, "content": "This is the pattern for a custom-schema project with API tests + table tests. It uses `environment: table_test` for the table test package and creates `connectors/sources_table_test.sqrl` only if there are mutation tables (not our case). Since we have no mutation, the table-test package just sets environment table_test? Wait, environment table_test would need a `consumer_loans-table_test.sqrl` connector file in the catalog \u2014 not available! Since the catalog only has test/prod. Hmm. But step 5 of the skill says if no mutation table, stop (don't create sources_table_test). But then environment \"table_test\" must resolve to some connector. In library_loans, environment is a local concept mapping to `connectors/sources-{{environment}}`. The table_test env likely falls back? Let me check library_loans connectors.\n\nActually for our project, the include resolves `consumer_loans-{{environment}}`. We could set the table-test package's environment to `test` so it uses the catalog test connectors. But then it's identical to the API test env. The skill's step 5 (mutation case) sets environment table_test to point at local mutation-free sources. Since we have no mutation, we can keep `environment: test` in the table-test package and still use `use-inferred-schema: true`. The only reason for table_test env is to swap mutation sources.\n\nHmm, but the table-test package needs `script.include` too? It layers the shared base which has include. Good. It sets `script.config.environment` to... The shared base has no environment; the API test package sets test. If table test package layers shared + table-test package, and table-test sets environment test, that's fine. Actually the run-tests suite line layers `library_loans-shared-package.json library_loans-table-test-package.json`. Both need environment set. If table-test doesn't set it, `{{environment}}` unresolved in the consumer's import. So set it to `test`.\n\nWait, but the shared base has `script.include.data_catalog` with package ontology-test-package.json. Good.\n\nAlso note library_loans shared base enables kafka because it has a mutation table. We don't, so we drop kafka.\n\nNow ENVS=\"test prod\" and SUBPROJECTS=\"loan_payments loan_payments_table_test\". Suite table:\n- loan_payments/test: shared + api-test package\n- loan_payments/prod: shared + prod package\n- loan_payments_table_test/test: shared + table-test package\n- loan_payments_table_test/prod: ? The skill example only has table_test/test. Let me check library_loans suite full.\n\nLet me see lines 184-192 of library_loans run-tests.sh."}}
