{"request_uuid": "ce794cda-7704-4462-a744-ff62d48b00d8", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T08:46:16.773470+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "planning", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cbbfe167ac1a849f688", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "---\ndomains:\n  - finance\nscenario: pipeline\n---\n\n# Implementation Plan: Personal Loan Payments API\n\n**Scenario**: pipeline\n**Task**: new-project\n**Date**: 2026-11-24T08:44:55Z\n**Status**: DRAFT\n\nA new DataSQRL pipeline in `loan-payments/` that reads the shared `data-catalog` consumer-loan\nsources, builds a per-loan payment summary and a per-payment table, and serves them through a\nJWT-authorized GraphQL/REST/MCP API. It reuses the catalog connectors, its test data and the\nproject layout of the sibling `lending/` project, and adds no data of its own.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Source\nThe specification lives in `adr/requirements_20261124-113440.md`: goal and scope, `### Sources`,\n`### Time semantics`, `### Entities and keys`, `### Transformations and aggregations`,\n`### API surface`, `### Test data and acceptance criteria`, `### Non-functional requirements`,\n`### Hard constraints`, and `### Open Questions`. Build the project to satisfy `FR-1`\u2013`FR-13`\nand the acceptance criteria there; the payload shapes and expected test values are quoted there\nand are not repeated in this plan.\n\nThe sibling `lending/` project (`lending/lending360.sqrl`, `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`,\n`lending/lending360-test-package.json`, `lending/lending360-prod-package.json`, and its\n`lending/lending360-api/` folder) is the layout and API-configuration reference. The shared\n`data-catalog` module (sibling directory, read-only) supplies the source tables `Personal_Loan`\nand `Loan_Payment` and their test data; the project imports them and never copies or edits them.\n\n## Implementation Checklist\nLegend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n\n- [ ] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n- [ ] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n- [ ] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n- [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [ ] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table: import the catalog consumer-loan scripts, keep the latest version of each loan and payment by `source_updated_at`, retain only `loan_type = 'PERSONAL'` payments, and enrich them from their loan record (FR-1\u2013FR-5, `### Transformations and aggregations` items 1\u20133). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [ ] 7. Implement `LoanPaymentSummary` anchored on all latest personal loans and left-joined to the applied-payment aggregates, so only `APPLIED` payments contribute totals and a loan with no payments gets zero counts and a null last payment date (FR-6, FR-7, FR-8). [deps: 6] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [ ] 8. Add the three authorization-filtered lookups \u2014 summary by `loan_id`, payments by `loan_id`, and the signed-in customer's loans with their summaries \u2014 reading the `customer_id` claim (FR-9\u2013FR-12). [deps: 4, 7] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl, /design-api\n- [ ] 9. Review the completed pipeline for data-quality and observability gaps and add tables only where a credible failure is unguarded; otherwise record why nothing new is needed (see `## Data Quality & Observability`). [deps: 8] \u2192 skill: /monitor-pipeline\n- [ ] 10. Add a separate inferred-schema table-test package covering the data-integrity criteria: personal-only row count, absence of `AL-` loan ids, and one row per `payment_id` and per `loan_id` (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 11. Add API tests in the custom-schema test package for the snapshot criteria and JWT cases: the returned payment, a loan with applied late fees, the zero-payment loan, the four-loan customer, a wrong customer, and a missing token (acceptance criteria for FR-5\u2013FR-13). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 12. Create `run-tests.sh` declaring the `test`/`prod` environments and both test suites, then run it and regenerate the snapshots. [deps: 10, 11] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 13. Document the project, its sources, its API, the authorization model, and how FR-8 is covered in the README. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /write-documentation\n- [ ] 14. [cond: tests fail after step 12] Diagnose and fix the failing compile or snapshot. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /troubleshoot-test\n\n## Data Quality & Observability\n- **Build** \u2014 none new. The one credible silent-loss point is the inner join from personal\n  payments to `Personal_Loan`: a `PERSONAL` payment whose loan record never arrives would vanish\n  from `LoanPayments` and undercount its summary. The catalog already guarantees this cannot\n  happen (`LoanPaymentReferencesValidPersonalLoan_Test` in\n  `data-catalog/lending/lending-ontology.sqrl`), so no capture table is warranted. FR-8 is handled\n  by construction (latest-version dedup feeding an unwindowed re-aggregation), not by monitoring.\n- **Skip** \u2014 do not repeat the catalog's referential-integrity, enum, or numeric-sanity assertions;\n  do not add ingestion counters for the two sources, because the independent-sender failure mode\n  does not apply and the catalog's root snapshot queries already surface content changes; do not\n  monitor the intentional auto-loan exclusion, which is a required filter, not an anomaly.\n- **Reuse** \u2014 the catalog's lending-ontology assertions and root-ontology snapshot queries, and the\n  `lending/` project's convention of carrying no pipeline-local DQ tables.\n\n## Technical Decisions\n- A custom GraphQL schema plus operations (not an inferred schema) is used, because `customer_id`\n  must be injected from the JWT rather than accepted from the caller and the exposed type names are\n  fixed; the API is configured like `lending/lending360-api/`.\n- The engine set is Flink + Postgres + Vert.x. No `kafka` engine is enabled: the API has no mutation\n  or subscription, and the catalog's Kafka sources are external Flink connectors that do not need\n  the DataSQRL-managed Kafka engine.\n- The catalog is included under `script.include` through one of its top-level package files with\n  `is_batch` false, exactly like `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`; the consumer's\n  per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the `-test` or `-prod` connector file it\n  imports, so the include's own environment never reaches the running pipeline.\n- CDC streams are reduced with `DISTINCT ... ON <key> ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`, and the\n  summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the\n  streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n- `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n  aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n  Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions/relationships over an internal\n  summary/state table, with a Vert.x `auth` issuer/key block per environment; the `NOT NULL` claim\n  argument produces the required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n\n## Assumptions\n**FR-8 coverage**: Assumed FR-8 is verified by construction \u2014 the latest-version `DISTINCT` feeds an\nunwindowed re-aggregation \u2014 and documented in the README instead of by a snapshot. Rationale: no\ncatalog payment changes status, and the scope forbids adding synthetic source data of our own.\n[impact: low]\n\n**Catalog include config**: Assumed the catalog is included with one of its top-level package files\nand `is_batch` false (as `lending/` does) while the consumer's `environment` selects the connector\nfile. Rationale: the consumer imports only the `-{{environment}}` connector, so the include's own\nenvironment setting is inert. [impact: medium]\n\n**Freshness**: Assumed new or changed payments appear within one minute through the streaming Flink\npipeline with no window. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`, and the\ncatalog watermarks (10 s test, 30 s prod) are used as-is. [impact: high]\n\n**JWT validation**: Assumed HS256 with a fixed test secret in `test` and a key from `${JWT_SECRET}`\nin `prod`, with issuer and audience supplied as environment variables. Rationale: the recommended\ndefault in `### Open Questions`. [impact: high]\n\n**Production workload**: Assumed up to 1,000,000 personal loans, 50,000 payments per day, and a\n50 requests/second peak. Rationale: the recommended default; it only affects deployment sizing.\n[impact: medium]\n\n**Dev/local environment**: Assumed only `test` and `prod` overlays, because the scope names exactly\nthose two and follows `lending/`. [impact: low]\n\n**Loans without payments**: Assumed `LoanPaymentSummary` returns a row for every personal loan, with\nzero counts/sums and a null `last_payment_date` when no applied payment exists. Rationale: the\nrecommended default and the acceptance criterion for `PL-011`. [impact: medium]\n\n**Loan status**: Assumed the API exposes loans in every status, not only `ACTIVE`. Rationale: the\nrecommended default, and the scope keeps all statuses. [impact: medium]\n\n**Last payment date**: Assumed the latest `applied_date` among applied payments. Rationale: the\nrecommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**Total amount paid**: Assumed `total_paid_cents` is the sum of `payment_amount_cents` of applied\npayments. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**Customer-query loan details**: Assumed the signed-in customer's loans also show `loan_status`,\n`original_amount_cents`, `current_balance_cents`, `monthly_payment_cents` and\n`next_payment_due_date`. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**API protocols**: Assumed GraphQL, REST and MCP, matching `lending/`. Rationale: the recommended\ndefault and `### API surface`. [impact: low]\n\n**Budget**: Assumed the smallest DataSQRL Cloud deployment size. Rationale: the recommended default;\nno budget was given. [impact: low]\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 6, "timestamp": 1795509976773}}
{"request_uuid": "ce794cda-7704-4462-a744-ff62d48b00d8", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T08:46:16.774001+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "planning", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Now verify no PENDING markers survive and read the file.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cbbfdda7b81bbe227fc", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "grep -n \"PENDING\" /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md; echo \"exit:$?\""}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cbbfe167ac1a849f688", "name": "read", "arguments": {"path": "/workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 85, "output": 127, "cacheRead": 114688, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 12, "totalTokens": 114900, "cost": {"input": 2.55e-05, "output": 0.0001524, "cacheRead": 0.000688128, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.000866028}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795509975141, "responseId": "dcae4070e65e4418a0fb55a7ab446d7d-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 1623, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cbbfdda7b81bbe227fc", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "exit:1\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 7, "timestamp": 1795509976772}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cbbfe167ac1a849f688", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "---\ndomains:\n  - finance\nscenario: pipeline\n---\n\n# Implementation Plan: Personal Loan Payments API\n\n**Scenario**: pipeline\n**Task**: new-project\n**Date**: 2026-11-24T08:44:55Z\n**Status**: DRAFT\n\nA new DataSQRL pipeline in `loan-payments/` that reads the shared `data-catalog` consumer-loan\nsources, builds a per-loan payment summary and a per-payment table, and serves them through a\nJWT-authorized GraphQL/REST/MCP API. It reuses the catalog connectors, its test data and the\nproject layout of the sibling `lending/` project, and adds no data of its own.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Source\nThe specification lives in `adr/requirements_20261124-113440.md`: goal and scope, `### Sources`,\n`### Time semantics`, `### Entities and keys`, `### Transformations and aggregations`,\n`### API surface`, `### Test data and acceptance criteria`, `### Non-functional requirements`,\n`### Hard constraints`, and `### Open Questions`. Build the project to satisfy `FR-1`\u2013`FR-13`\nand the acceptance criteria there; the payload shapes and expected test values are quoted there\nand are not repeated in this plan.\n\nThe sibling `lending/` project (`lending/lending360.sqrl`, `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`,\n`lending/lending360-test-package.json`, `lending/lending360-prod-package.json`, and its\n`lending/lending360-api/` folder) is the layout and API-configuration reference. The shared\n`data-catalog` module (sibling directory, read-only) supplies the source tables `Personal_Loan`\nand `Loan_Payment` and their test data; the project imports them and never copies or edits them.\n\n## Implementation Checklist\nLegend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n\n- [ ] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n- [ ] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n- [ ] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n- [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [ ] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table: import the catalog consumer-loan scripts, keep the latest version of each loan and payment by `source_updated_at`, retain only `loan_type = 'PERSONAL'` payments, and enrich them from their loan record (FR-1\u2013FR-5, `### Transformations and aggregations` items 1\u20133). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [ ] 7. Implement `LoanPaymentSummary` anchored on all latest personal loans and left-joined to the applied-payment aggregates, so only `APPLIED` payments contribute totals and a loan with no payments gets zero counts and a null last payment date (FR-6, FR-7, FR-8). [deps: 6] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [ ] 8. Add the three authorization-filtered lookups \u2014 summary by `loan_id`, payments by `loan_id`, and the signed-in customer's loans with their summaries \u2014 reading the `customer_id` claim (FR-9\u2013FR-12). [deps: 4, 7] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl, /design-api\n- [ ] 9. Review the completed pipeline for data-quality and observability gaps and add tables only where a credible failure is unguarded; otherwise record why nothing new is needed (see `## Data Quality & Observability`). [deps: 8] \u2192 skill: /monitor-pipeline\n- [ ] 10. Add a separate inferred-schema table-test package covering the data-integrity criteria: personal-only row count, absence of `AL-` loan ids, and one row per `payment_id` and per `loan_id` (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 11. Add API tests in the custom-schema test package for the snapshot criteria and JWT cases: the returned payment, a loan with applied late fees, the zero-payment loan, the four-loan customer, a wrong customer, and a missing token (acceptance criteria for FR-5\u2013FR-13). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 12. Create `run-tests.sh` declaring the `test`/`prod` environments and both test suites, then run it and regenerate the snapshots. [deps: 10, 11] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [ ] 13. Document the project, its sources, its API, the authorization model, and how FR-8 is covered in the README. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /write-documentation\n- [ ] 14. [cond: tests fail after step 12] Diagnose and fix the failing compile or snapshot. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /troubleshoot-test\n\n## Data Quality & Observability\n- **Build** \u2014 none new. The one credible silent-loss point is the inner join from personal\n  payments to `Personal_Loan`: a `PERSONAL` payment whose loan record never arrives would vanish\n  from `LoanPayments` and undercount its summary. The catalog already guarantees this cannot\n  happen (`LoanPaymentReferencesValidPersonalLoan_Test` in\n  `data-catalog/lending/lending-ontology.sqrl`), so no capture table is warranted. FR-8 is handled\n  by construction (latest-version dedup feeding an unwindowed re-aggregation), not by monitoring.\n- **Skip** \u2014 do not repeat the catalog's referential-integrity, enum, or numeric-sanity assertions;\n  do not add ingestion counters for the two sources, because the independent-sender failure mode\n  does not apply and the catalog's root snapshot queries already surface content changes; do not\n  monitor the intentional auto-loan exclusion, which is a required filter, not an anomaly.\n- **Reuse** \u2014 the catalog's lending-ontology assertions and root-ontology snapshot queries, and the\n  `lending/` project's convention of carrying no pipeline-local DQ tables.\n\n## Technical Decisions\n- A custom GraphQL schema plus operations (not an inferred schema) is used, because `customer_id`\n  must be injected from the JWT rather than accepted from the caller and the exposed type names are\n  fixed; the API is configured like `lending/lending360-api/`.\n- The engine set is Flink + Postgres + Vert.x. No `kafka` engine is enabled: the API has no mutation\n  or subscription, and the catalog's Kafka sources are external Flink connectors that do not need\n  the DataSQRL-managed Kafka engine.\n- The catalog is included under `script.include` through one of its top-level package files with\n  `is_batch` false, exactly like `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`; the consumer's\n  per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the `-test` or `-prod` connector file it\n  imports, so the include's own environment never reaches the running pipeline.\n- CDC streams are reduced with `DISTINCT ... ON <key> ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`, and the\n  summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the\n  streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n- `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n  aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n  Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions/relationships over an internal\n  summary/state table, with a Vert.x `auth` issuer/key block per environment; the `NOT NULL` claim\n  argument produces the required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n\n## Assumptions\n**FR-8 coverage**: Assumed FR-8 is verified by construction \u2014 the latest-version `DISTINCT` feeds an\nunwindowed re-aggregation \u2014 and documented in the README instead of by a snapshot. Rationale: no\ncatalog payment changes status, and the scope forbids adding synthetic source data of our own.\n[impact: low]\n\n**Catalog include config**: Assumed the catalog is included with one of its top-level package files\nand `is_batch` false (as `lending/` does) while the consumer's `environment` selects the connector\nfile. Rationale: the consumer imports only the `-{{environment}}` connector, so the include's own\nenvironment setting is inert. [impact: medium]\n\n**Freshness**: Assumed new or changed payments appear within one minute through the streaming Flink\npipeline with no window. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`, and the\ncatalog watermarks (10 s test, 30 s prod) are used as-is. [impact: high]\n\n**JWT validation**: Assumed HS256 with a fixed test secret in `test` and a key from `${JWT_SECRET}`\nin `prod`, with issuer and audience supplied as environment variables. Rationale: the recommended\ndefault in `### Open Questions`. [impact: high]\n\n**Production workload**: Assumed up to 1,000,000 personal loans, 50,000 payments per day, and a\n50 requests/second peak. Rationale: the recommended default; it only affects deployment sizing.\n[impact: medium]\n\n**Dev/local environment**: Assumed only `test` and `prod` overlays, because the scope names exactly\nthose two and follows `lending/`. [impact: low]\n\n**Loans without payments**: Assumed `LoanPaymentSummary` returns a row for every personal loan, with\nzero counts/sums and a null `last_payment_date` when no applied payment exists. Rationale: the\nrecommended default and the acceptance criterion for `PL-011`. [impact: medium]\n\n**Loan status**: Assumed the API exposes loans in every status, not only `ACTIVE`. Rationale: the\nrecommended default, and the scope keeps all statuses. [impact: medium]\n\n**Last payment date**: Assumed the latest `applied_date` among applied payments. Rationale: the\nrecommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**Total amount paid**: Assumed `total_paid_cents` is the sum of `payment_amount_cents` of applied\npayments. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**Customer-query loan details**: Assumed the signed-in customer's loans also show `loan_status`,\n`original_amount_cents`, `current_balance_cents`, `monthly_payment_cents` and\n`next_payment_due_date`. Rationale: the recommended default in `### Open Questions`. [impact: low]\n\n**API protocols**: Assumed GraphQL, REST and MCP, matching `lending/`. Rationale: the recommended\ndefault and `### API surface`. [impact: low]\n\n**Budget**: Assumed the smallest DataSQRL Cloud deployment size. Rationale: the recommended default;\nno budget was given. [impact: low]\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 6, "timestamp": 1795509976773}]}
