figuration field names in prose are probably fine, but to be safe I could describe them without JSON syntax. The checklist already uses `script.include`; the task-context itself uses these in examples. Hmm. The strict rule: don't write statements. I'll revise Technical Decisions to avoid the SQRL clause and JSON. Keep it prose.\n\nLet me revise the CDC bullet and include bullet, and Authorization bullet.\n\nAlso the checklist step 7 mentions \"left-joined to the applied-payment aggregates\" \u2014 prose, fine. Step 6 mentions `source_updated_at` and `loan_type='PERSONAL'` \u2014 these are column names from the catalog, not created by implementation, and referencing requirements. Fine.\n\nLet me edit Technical Decisions to remove code-like syntax:\n- CDC bullet: \"CDC streams are reduced to the latest version per key ordered by the source update timestamp, and the summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\"\n- include bullet: \"The catalog is included through one of its top-level package files with the batch mode disabled, exactly like the sibling `lending/` base config; the consumer's per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the test or prod connector file it imports...\" \u2014 `script.config.environment` is a config field name in prose, acceptable. Maybe say \"per-environment engine configuration\". I'll keep one config path mention minimal but acceptable. Actually to be safe, say \"the consumer's per-environment configuration selects which connector file it imports\". Fine.\n- Authorization bullet: \"Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions and relationships over an internal state table, with a per-environment auth provider; the required claim argument produces the authorization error when the claim is absent.\" Avoid `NOT NULL`.\n- Also `DISTINCT` in DQ section: \"latest-version dedup\" is fine (I wrote \"latest-version dedup\"). Good.\n\nAlso \"FR-8 coverage\" assumption mentions \"latest-version `DISTINCT`\" \u2014 that's in Assumptions, not the three restricted sections. Rule only restricts checklist, technical decisions, DQ. Assumptions can be freer. But still no need. I'll leave.\n\nLet me also reconsider: The Data Quality section mentions `LoanPaymentReferencesValidPersonalLoan_Test` \u2014 a table name, fine. It's not SQL.\n\nLet me make the edits.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The plan is complete. Let me refine the Technical Decisions to keep it as prose (no SQRL/SQL/config statements), per the section content rule."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cbc0b9a73d1a9611413", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "- The catalog is included through one of its top-level package files with the batch mode disabled,\n  exactly like the sibling `lending/` base config; the consumer's per-environment configuration\n  selects which catalog connector file it imports, so the included module's own environment setting\n  never reaches the running pipeline.\n- CDC streams are reduced to the latest version per key ordered by the source update timestamp, and\n  the summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within\n  the streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n- `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n  aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n  Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions and relationships over an internal\n  state table, with a per-environment Vert.x auth provider; a required claim argument produces the\n  required authorization error when the claim is absent.", "oldText": "- The catalog is included under `script.include` through one of its top-level package files with\n  `is_batch` false, exactly like `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`; the consumer's\n  per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the `-test` or `-prod` connector file it\n  imports, so the include's own environment never reaches the running pipeline.\n- CDC streams are reduced with `DISTINCT ... ON <key> ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`, and the\n  summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the\n  streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n- `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n  aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n  Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions/relationships over an internal\n  summary/state table, with a Vert.x `auth` issuer/key block per environment; the `NOT NULL` claim\n  argument produces the required authorization error when the claim is absent."}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 2870, "output": 1518, "cacheRead": 114816, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 906, "totalTokens": 119204, "cost": {"input": 0.000861, "output": 0.0018215999999999998, "cacheRead": 0.000688896, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.003371496}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795509976775, "responseId": "8ddc1f74b99048408d6fb44495edf90f-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 6643, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cbc0b9a73d1a9611413", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  70   fixed; the API is configured like `lending/lending360-api/`.\n  71 - The engine set is Flink + Postgres + Vert.x. No `kafka` engine is enabled: the API has no mutation\n  72   or subscription, and the catalog's Kafka sources are external Flink connectors that do not need\n  73   the DataSQRL-managed Kafka engine.\n- 74 - The catalog is included under `script.include` through one of its top-level package files with\n- 75   `is_batch` false, exactly like `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`; the consumer's\n- 76   per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the `-test` or `-prod` connector file it\n- 77   imports, so the include's own environment never reaches the running pipeline.\n- 78 - CDC streams are reduced with `DISTINCT ... ON <key> ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`, and the\n- 79   summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the\n- 80   streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n+ 74 - The catalog is included through one of its top-level package files with the batch mode disabled,\n+ 75   exactly like the sibling `lending/` base config; the consumer's per-environment configuration\n+ 76   selects which catalog connector file it imports, so the included module's own environment setting\n+ 77   never reaches the running pipeline.\n+ 78 - CDC streams are reduced to the latest version per key ordered by the source update timestamp, and\n+ 79   the summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within\n+ 80   the streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n  81 - `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n  82   aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n  83   Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n- 84 - Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions/relationships over an internal\n- 85   summary/state table, with a Vert.x `auth` issuer/key block per environment; the `NOT NULL` claim\n- 86   argument produces the required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n+ 84 - Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions and relationships over an internal\n+ 85   state table, with a per-environment Vert.x auth provider; a required claim argument produces the\n+ 86   required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n  87 \n  88 ## Assumptions\n  89 **FR-8 coverage**: Assumed FR-8 is verified by construction \u2014 the latest-version `DISTINCT` feeds an\n  90 unwindowed re-aggregation \u2014 and documented in the README instead of by a snapshot. Rationale: no\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n@@ -70,21 +70,21 @@\n   fixed; the API is configured like `lending/lending360-api/`.\n - The engine set is Flink + Postgres + Vert.x. No `kafka` engine is enabled: the API has no mutation\n   or subscription, and the catalog's Kafka sources are external Flink connectors that do not need\n   the DataSQRL-managed Kafka engine.\n-- The catalog is included under `script.include` through one of its top-level package files with\n-  `is_batch` false, exactly like `lending/lending360-shared-package.json`; the consumer's\n-  per-environment `script.config.environment` selects the `-test` or `-prod` connector file it\n-  imports, so the include's own environment never reaches the running pipeline.\n-- CDC streams are reduced with `DISTINCT ... ON <key> ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`, and the\n-  summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within the\n-  streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n+- The catalog is included through one of its top-level package files with the batch mode disabled,\n+  exactly like the sibling `lending/` base config; the consumer's per-environment configuration\n+  selects which catalog connector file it imports, so the included module's own environment setting\n+  never reaches the running pipeline.\n+- CDC streams are reduced to the latest version per key ordered by the source update timestamp, and\n+  the summary is an unwindowed re-aggregation, so a late or changed payment updates the API within\n+  the streaming freshness target instead of waiting for a window boundary.\n - `LoanPaymentSummary` is anchored on the latest personal loans and left-joins the applied-payment\n   aggregates. Grouping only the payments would omit the loans that have none, which the accepted\n   Open-Question default requires to appear with zero counts and a null last payment date.\n-- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions/relationships over an internal\n-  summary/state table, with a Vert.x `auth` issuer/key block per environment; the `NOT NULL` claim\n-  argument produces the required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n+- Authorization is implemented as claim-injected table functions and relationships over an internal\n+  state table, with a per-environment Vert.x auth provider; a required claim argument produces the\n+  required authorization error when the claim is absent.\n \n ## Assumptions\n **FR-8 coverage**: Assumed FR-8 is verified by construction \u2014 the latest-version `DISTINCT` feeds an\n unwindowed re-aggregation \u2014 and documented in the README instead of by a snapshot. Rationale: no\n", "firstChangedLine": 74}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 6, "timestamp": 1795509983425}]}
