EAMING\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n===API-TEST===\n{\n  \"script\": {\n    \"config\": { \"environment\": \"test\" }\n  },\n  \"test-runner\": {\n    \"use-inferred-schema\": false,\n    \"snapshot-folder\": \"snapshots/library_loans/\",\n    \"test-folder\": \"library_loans-api/tests/\",\n    \"delay-sec\": 30,\n    \"mutation-delay-sec\": 1\n  }\n}\n===TABLE-TEST===\n{\n  \"script\": {\n    \"config\": { \"environment\": \"table_test\" }\n  },\n  \"test-runner\": {\n    \"use-inferred-schema\": true,\n    \"snapshot-folder\": \"snapshots/library_loans_table_test/\",\n    \"test-folder\": \"no-graphql-tests/\",\n    \"delay-sec\": -1,\n    \"required-checkpoints\": 1\n  }\n}\n===PROD===\n{\n  \"script\": {\n    \"config\": { \"environment\": \"prod\" }\n  }\n}\n===SUITE===\n2:# This project's suites \u2014 one command, deterministic exit code.\n8:#   <sub-project>       zero or more names, in any order, selecting which suites run.\n14:#   --env <name>        which environment's configs to use (default: test).\n20:#                       line per suite \u2014 exactly the arguments a real run would use\n23:#   ./run-tests.sh                                     test every suite, env test\n25:#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env local               compile every suite as local\n36:#   Three blocks below are marked \"EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT\": the ENVS/SUBPROJECTS declarations,\n37:#   the `suite` table, and the optional setup/teardown hooks. Everything else is boilerplate \u2014\n40:#   The `suite` table is the ONE place a project's config layering is written down: for each\n89:# fails loudly instead of matching nothing, running zero suites and still exiting 0.\n90:ENVS=\"test prod\"\n91:SUBPROJECTS=\"library_loans library_loans_table_test\"\n101:    --test)      VERB=test ;;\n105:    --list-envs) echo \"$ENVS\"; exit 0 ;;\n106:    --list-subprojects) echo \"$SUBPROJECTS\"; exit 0 ;;\n112:case \" $ENVS \" in\n114:  *) echo \"unknown env '$ENV' \u2014 this project declares: $ENVS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n118:  case \" $SUBPROJECTS \" in\n120:    *) echo \"unknown sub-project '$s' \u2014 this project ships: $SUBPROJECTS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n130:# Each suite writes its own build folder (the -b flag in the driver loop below), so one suite's\n136:  # Every named config must exist. A missing one means the suite line and this environment\n170:# Anything the suites need first \u2014 generating or downloading test data too large for git,\n175:# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT: the suite table \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n178:# filenames out literally; any names work. Cover every pair of SUBPROJECTS x ENVS that this\n184:suite() {\n186:    library_loans/test)            echo \"library_loans-shared-package.json library_loans-api-test-package.json\"        ;;\n188:    library_loans_table_test/test) echo \"library_loans-shared-package.json library_loans-table-test-package.json\" ;;\n197:for sub in $SUBPROJECTS; do\n200:  args=\"$(suite \"$sub\" \"$ENV\")\" || {\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 9, "timestamp": 1795509950183}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "This is the pattern for a custom-schema project with API tests + table tests. It uses `environment: table_test` for the table test package and creates `connectors/sources_table_test.sqrl` only if there are mutation tables (not our case). Since we have no mutation, the table-test package just sets environment table_test? Wait, environment table_test would need a `consumer_loans-table_test.sqrl` connector file in the catalog \u2014 not available! Since the catalog only has test/prod. Hmm. But step 5 of the skill says if no mutation table, stop (don't create sources_table_test). But then environment \"table_test\" must resolve to some connector. In library_loans, environment is a local concept mapping to `connectors/sources-{{environment}}`. The table_test env likely falls back? Let me check library_loans connectors.\n\nActually for our project, the include resolves `consumer_loans-{{environment}}`. We could set the table-test package's environment to `test` so it uses the catalog test connectors. But then it's identical to the API test env. The skill's step 5 (mutation case) sets environment table_test to point at local mutation-free sources. Since we have no mutation, we can keep `environment: test` in the table-test package and still use `use-inferred-schema: true`. The only reason for table_test env is to swap mutation sources.\n\nHmm, but the table-test package needs `script.include` too? It layers the shared base which has include. Good. It sets `script.config.environment` to... The shared base has no environment; the API test package sets test. If table test package layers shared + table-test package, and table-test sets environment test, that's fine. Actually the run-tests suite line layers `library_loans-shared-package.json library_loans-table-test-package.json`. Both need environment set. If table-test doesn't set it, `{{environment}}` unresolved in the consumer's import. So set it to `test`.\n\nWait, but the shared base has `script.include.data_catalog` with package ontology-test-package.json. Good.\n\nAlso note library_loans shared base enables kafka because it has a mutation table. We don't, so we drop kafka.\n\nNow ENVS=\"test prod\" and SUBPROJECTS=\"loan_payments loan_payments_table_test\". Suite table:\n- loan_payments/test: shared + api-test package\n- loan_payments/prod: shared + prod package\n- loan_payments_table_test/test: shared + table-test package\n- loan_payments_table_test/prod: ? The skill example only has table_test/test. Let me check library_loans suite full.\n\nLet me see lines 184-192 of library_loans run-tests.sh.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cbba24f7ed192303185", "na